  "id": "Compound::DB00701 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Amprenavir is linked to Cyp2d6 through a dual mechanism involving cytochrome P450 3a4 (CYP3A4) enzymes. The evidence suggests that Amprenavir, as an inhibitor of CYP3A4, indirectly affects Cyp2d6 by modulating the activity of this enzyme. This is supported by the inclusion of Amprenavir in the category of CYP3A4 inhibitors, which in turn includes Efavirenz, a known inhibitor of Cyp2d6. The binding of Efavirenz to Cyp2d6 further establishes a direct interaction between the two entities. Additionally, the presence of Amprenavir in the category of CYP3A4 inducers, which includes Enzalutamide, provides an alternative pathway where Amprenavir might influence Cyp2d6 through enzyme induction. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between Amprenavir and Cyp2d6, emphasizing the role of CYP3A4 in mediating the relationship.",
